Apple released iOS 27.2, uniting the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-duo/">iPhone Duo</a> and other iPhone models on the same version of iOS. iOS 27.2 is the first major <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a> update, and it adds several useful new features.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/iOS-27.2-Next-to-iPhone.jpg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065585" /><br/>
<h2>Siri AI Improvements</h2><br/>
<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/siri/">Siri</a> AI can recall past conversations you had with it, so you can ask &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; about something it told you before, like a restaurant it previously recommended. It's also able to draw on more sources:<br/>
<ul><br/>
 	<li><a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/photos/">Photos</a> attached to Messages</li><br/>
 	<li>Calendar event attendees</li><br/>
 	<li>Voicemails</li><br/>
</ul><br/>
Apple says you'll also get better results from Safari history and Reading List.<br/>
<br/>
There's a redesigned Excluded Apps feature that lets you quickly select which apps &zwnj;Siri&zwnj;, Search, and suggestions can access. The prior App Access feature required excluding apps individually.<br/>
<br/>
There's also granular text selection, so you can select and copy just the part of a &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; response you need.<br/>
<br/>
&zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI requires an iPhone 15 Pro or later.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Siri AI Languages</h2><br/>
&zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI is now available in more languages, including French, Japanese, Korean, Portuguese, and Spanish. &zwnj;Siri&zwnj; AI is still not available in the EU or mainland China.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Messages</h2><br/>
Suggestions in Messages have been added in iOS 27.2. The feature was available during the &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj; beta testing period, but was removed before launch.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/06/iOS-27-Messages-Notes-Suggestion.jpeg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1052829" /><br/>
Messages suggestions show tappable shortcuts in a conversation based on context, so you can do things like track a package with a tap, or add a dinner invite to the Calendar app.<br/>
<br/>
You can choose the suggestions you want, with options to add Calendar, Reminders, Notes, Maps, and Flights and Packages.<br/>
<h2>Apple Music</h2><br/>
iOS 27.2 introduces a new <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-music/">Apple Music</a> icon that goes with Apple's recent &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj; rebranding. The icon is black and white, replacing the red icon. Apple also changed the color of the highlights in the navigation bar and other areas of the &zwnj;Apple Music&zwnj; app to remove the red color.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1070915" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/apple-music-icon-1.jpg" alt="" width="1600" height="900" /><br/>
<h2>Photos</h2><br/>
Shared Albums in the &zwnj;Photos&zwnj; app now have an edit option for captions and comments. Apple also added a feature for avoiding duplicate photos, and there's now a reminder before albums expire so users can save important photos and videos.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>SynthID</h2><br/>
<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/26/iphone-synthid-watermarks/">iOS 27.2 includes SynthID labeling</a> for <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/image-playground/">Image Playground</a> images and some &zwnj;Photos&zwnj; app edits. Watermarks are added when using Extend and Reframe in &zwnj;Photos&zwnj;, and for large edits with the Clean Up tool. You can check images for SynthID using Google's <a href="https://synthid.com/">SynthID Detector website</a>.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/10/google-synthid.jpg" alt="" width="1920" height="1080" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1069339" /><br/>
<br/>
<h2>Podcasts</h2><br/>
The Home tab in the Podcasts app has separate sections for New Episodes and Continue Playing. The new sections replace Up Next.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065636" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/ios-27-2-podcasts.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" /><br/>
<br/>
<h2>Games</h2><br/>
The Friends tab in the Games app now includes context on friend suggestions and shows recent games played on friends' player pages.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Apple TV</h2><br/>
<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/apple-tv/">Apple TV</a> app users can now create profiles in the account settings section on the iPhone and <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipad/">iPad</a>. Profiles only require a name, profile rating, and information about whether the user is a child.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065602" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/ios-27-2-tv-app-profiles.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" /><br/>
<br/>
Creating a profile for a child limits content to a PG rating by default, but there is a customize option for finer control. Users can select age ratings for TV shows and movies that are appropriate for the child based on their age.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Phone</h2><br/>
The Call Context feature in the Phone app <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/09/16/ios-27-2-could-save-your-marriage/">reminds you of a contact's anniversary</a> when you call them, as long as you've saved the date in the Contacts app.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065607" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/ios272anniversary.jpg" alt="" width="1400" height="788" /><br/>
<br/>
<h2>FaceTime</h2><br/>
<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/facetime/">FaceTime</a> Dual Capture is now available in group &zwnj;FaceTime&zwnj; calls. Dual Capture is a feature that lets you stream &zwnj;FaceTime&zwnj; video content from the front and rear cameras at the same time. On a compatible device running &zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj;, flipping the camera while on a &zwnj;FaceTime&zwnj; call automatically turns on Dual Capture.<br/>
<br/>
Dual Capture is available on the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-17/">iPhone 17</a>, &zwnj;iPhone 17&zwnj; Pro, &zwnj;iPhone 17&zwnj; Pro Max, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-air/">iPhone Air</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/iphone-18-pro/">iPhone 18 Pro</a>, &zwnj;iPhone 18 Pro&zwnj; Max, and &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;.<br/>
<br/>
Apple also added an option to add a third-party sign language interpreter or live captioner to a call.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Shortcuts</h2><br/>
&zwnj;iOS 27&zwnj; includes new automations, actions, and improvements for the Shortcuts app. There's a new "when my iPhone is opened or closed" automation for the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;.<br/>
<br/>
An updated Workout automation adds support for the Fitness app, and the App automation can provide the name of the app that was closed.<br/>
<br/>
Window layout can be configured with the "Show Actions" and Show Describe a Shortcut" menu items, and Shortcut names and icons can be edited from the library.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>iPhone Duo Updates</h2><br/>
iOS 27.2 adds <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/guide/apple-pencil/">Apple Pencil</a> USB-C support to the &zwnj;iPhone Duo&zwnj;. It also includes Edge Light to illuminate your face during video calls.<br/>
<br/>
<div class="center-wrap"><iframe title="Apple Pencil on iPhone Duo: Is It Useful?" src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/7xpgdj7Rbjk" width="560" height="315" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="allowfullscreen"></iframe></div><br/>
<h2>Multiview</h2><br/>
iOS 27.2 <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/26/ios-27-2-multiview-support/">expands Multiview</a> in the &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; app to the iPhone, so users can watch up to four live sports streams simultaneously.<br/>
<br/>
Multiview works for sports events included in an &zwnj;Apple TV&zwnj; subscription: Major League Soccer (MLS), Formula 1 (F1) in the U.S., and Friday Night Baseball doubleheaders during the Major League Baseball season.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Clock App</h2><br/>
There are smaller a.m. and p.m. labels in the alarm list in the Clock app.<br/>
<br/>
<img class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1065633" src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/09/ios-27-2-clock-app.jpg" alt="" width="2000" height="1125" /><br/>
<br/>
<h2>EU - App Tracking Transparency</h2><br/>
App Tracking Transparency supports an alternative expanded prompt for EU users along with re-prompting on an annual basis. The alternative prompt is required for users in France, Germany, Italy, Poland, and Romania.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Health App</h2><br/>
Apple tested its redesigned Health app in the iOS 27.2 beta, but it won't be coming out until later this year and is not included in iOS 27.2.<br/>
<br/>
<h2>Security Fixes</h2><br/>
iOS 27.2 addresses <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/26/ios-27-2-security-fixes/">more than 160 security vulnerabilities</a>. None of the vulnerabilities were actively exploited, but it's always a good idea to update when this many fixes are included.<div class="linkback">Related Roundups: <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ios-27/">iOS 27</a>, <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/ipados-27/">iPadOS 27</a></div><div class="linkback">Related Forum: <a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/forums/ios-27.251">iOS 27</a></div><br/>This article, &quot;<a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/10/26/ios-27-2-features/">iOS 27.2 Features: Everything New in iOS 27.2</a>&quot; first appeared on <a href="https://www.macrumors.com">MacRumors.com</a><br/><br/><a href="https://forums.macrumors.com/threads/ios-27-2-features-everything-new-in-ios-27-2.2492888/">Discuss this article</a> in our forums<br/><br/>